# What `vercel deploy` uploads from this directory: the API function and
# nothing else.
#
# Why it exists: the Vercel CLI's built-in ignore list covers `.env.local` and
# `.env.*.local` but **not `.env`**, so a deploy run from a working copy would
# upload the local `.env` -- the provider key with it -- to the build. A
# git-connected deploy never sees `.env` (it is git-ignored and was never
# committed); a CLI deploy reads the directory, and this file is what stands
# between the two.
#
# Deny by default, then allow back exactly what `api/index.py` needs: the
# entrypoint and its manifest, the package it imports from `src/`, the hashed
# lock the manifest points at, and the vector index hybrid retrieval loads.
# Anything new added to the repository stays out until it is listed here.

/*
!/api
!/src
!/requirements-api.txt
!/vercel.json
!/data
/data/*
!/data/kb_vectors.db

# Re-excluded inside the paths allowed back above.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

# Stated outright, although `/*` already covers them at the root: these must
# never be uploaded from anywhere in the tree.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.key
**/*.pem
